talic>- and <italic>y</italic>-axis.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="95-6603308f3"/></fig><fig id="fig4"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Effects of ZD6126 against CAL33 human head and neck xenografts (filled triangles indicate the time of treatment). Bars represent standard error of the mean.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="95-6603308f4"/></fig><fig id="fig5"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>(<bold>A</bold>) Effects of ZD6126 and gefitinib or ZD6126&#x0002b;gefitinib on CAL33 tumour xenografts (filled triangles and arrows indicate the time of treatments). Bars represent standard error of the mean. (<bold>B</bold>) Effects of ZD6126&#x0002b;gefitinib&#x0002b;RT on CAL33 tumour xenografts (filled triangles and arrows indicate the time of treatments). Tumour growth curves of ZD6126&#x0002b;gefitinib and ZD6126&#x0002b;gefitinib&#x0002b;RT were superimposed. Bars represent standard error of the mean.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="95-6603308f5"/></fig><fig id="fig6"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Effects of ZD6126, gefitinib, RT, ZD6126&#x0002b;gefitinib and ZD6126&#x0002b;gefitinib&#x0002b;RT on the labelling frequency and intensity of CD31 (endothelial cell marker) and Ki67 (proliferation marker) in CAL33 tumour xenografts. The final score was the result of the examination of three fields per tumour, and between four and eight tumours were investigated. Labelling intensities are shown as 0&#x0003d;no, 1&#x0003d;slight, 2&#x0003d;medium, 3&#x0003d;strong and 4&#x0003d;very strong, with the sum of all values in one histogram being 100&#x00025;. Scoring was performed at the end of experiments on day 33.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="95-6603308f6"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1<